{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/load.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T13:34:01.715551Z","id":"7036d7cd330636687725cdc34e3222d4b55161ca5835b486de881ec6e04bbedb","body":{"detail":"provium/src/typed/load.rs resolves paths through module scopes and use declarations, and provium/src/typed/emit.rs infers local types from annotations, signatures and operations. A resolution or method-dispatch mistake that still elaborates in Lean would translate a different program; differential scenarios (provium/src/typed/verify.rs, `differential`) only sample behaviour.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"07c4be93dfc7afbe0ecc71ce16b575acf9e51db0ec0cfbc3dccac164776683a2"},"suggested_fix":"Cross-check resolved callee paths and inferred local types against rustc output for the captured build (for example -Zunpretty=thir-tree or a rustc_public driver), or prove the translation against a formal Rust semantics (CORRECTNESS_PLAN P10).","summary":"The typed backend's name resolution and local type inference are trusted, not checked against rustc","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
